plan FlowState
title   Flow State: the design record and build plan
status  proposed
goal
    Flow State combines statechart actors with keyed network data in one Runtime, for applications
    written mostly by AI coding agents. Machines own workflow; operations are plain requests; entity
    domains keep shared records coherent; Stories replay any behaviour deterministically; and
    everything structural compiles into one representation that the CLI and inspection read, so an
    agent can learn how an application works without reading much code ("truth is a compilation
    target").

    This Plan is the single owner of the design and of the build order. It replaces the thirteen
    capability Plans and the draft Rewrite Epic, now archived under workflow/plans/archive/rewrite
    and workflow/tasks/archive/Rewrite-capability. Each decision below says what it keeps from
    them, what it changes and what it deletes. The section-level detail of entity domains lives in
    flow/entity-domain.md, which @O6 adopts as normative. Every other file under workflow/plans/flow
    and workflow/plans/archive is supporting material or provenance with no authority.

    The existing packages/flow-state-rewrite source implements a superseded surface; @O13 says what
    is ported, rewritten and deleted. packages/flow-state stays frozen until @O14 cutover.
outcomes
    O1  Authoring: definitions and machines
        definition(config) and machine(definition, callback) return their values directly and throw
        one FlowError with canonical diagnostics when construction fails (@D8).

        A definition declares:

        - **id**: exact authored durable name
        - **states**: recursive tree of state names; compound states name a default
        - **events**: public events: Effect Schema field records (@D44)
        - **internalEvents**: events only the actor's own schedules, reactions and outcomes produce 
        (@D19)
        - **input, memory**: Schema field records (@D45)
        - **initial**: input to memory; required when memory is non-empty; runs once for a fresh 
        actor, never on restore (@D46)
        - **context**: provider selectors (Provider.select(selector)), each one upward read edge 
        (@D24)
        - **operations**: flat named record of resource, transaction, stream and domain handles

        A definition derives public Schemas: Event (a Schema.TaggedUnion with the _tag envelope),
        State (literals of state paths), Input, Memory and Snapshot, so boundaries decode and
        encode with Flow's own protocol (@D47). State tokens are typed objects with flattened paths
        (S.OPEN.EDITING), expose is(snapshot) and child(snapshot), and narrow snapshot types (@D20).

        Names keep the archived identity rules: nonempty, at most 256 UTF-8 bytes, no C0 controls,
        DEL, NUL or lone surrogates, exact spelling without Unicode normalisation, composite
        identity length-prefixed (@D9).

        A machine is configured with on handlers, activities, schedules and onContext reactions, all
        static data whose callbacks only compute values (@D1, @D2): targets, operations, outcome
        events and write targets are never chosen by a callback.
    O2  Turns: one ordered, atomic macrostep per accepted event
        Every input to an actor (public event, internal event, schedule, operation outcome, context
        wave, lifecycle fact) enters one FIFO mailbox and is decided in one macrostep:

        1. Find the nearest handler for the event from the active leaf upward. Within it, try
        transitions in authored order; a guard returns true or deny(code, context?) (@D21). When
        every transition at one level declines, try the parent's handler (fallthrough, @D18).
        2. Run updateMemory, then the actions, both against the same pre-turn snapshot.
        3. Apply the target (a typed state token, or "self" for no state change: no exit, no entry,
        @D17) and the memory patch; enter defaults outermost first.
        4. Validate the whole action batch; stage actor and store changes.
        5. Publish one committed cut of actor and store, then start or join asynchronous work.

        No handler, or every guard declining, changes nothing and publishes nothing. A defect in
        any authored callback before commit keeps prior truth, publishes one issue-only snapshot
        and does not retry. check(snapshot, event) returns Allowed | Denied | Unhandled by the same
        rules, with Denied collecting every { code, context } tried; it starts nothing (@D22).
        check on an internal event is a type error.

        Schedules replace timers (@D23): schedules: { name: { schedule, send, restartOn? } }, where
        schedule is a Duration.Input, an Effect Schedule or a function of { memory, now } returning
        one; send is an event or E.X.from(metadata). restartOn restarts only that schedule when its
        selected value changes, and a schedule with restartOn stays idle until the first change.
        Schedules run on the Runtime Clock with deterministic ordering for equal deadlines.

        Activities are continuing declarations per state (the root state for whole-lifetime work)
        with computed parameters and an optional when predicate. Identity is the declaration slot,
        operation kind, descriptor and canonical key: an equal identity keeps its work and original
        parameters, a changed one releases the old work exactly once. Activity parameters may read
        earlier activities' lanes in declaration order; a cycle is a construction error.

        onContext: [{ select, when?, event }] reacts to provider changes; select reads context and
        memory, only context waves re-trigger it, the first selection is silent, and event is a
        constructor or E.X.from(selected) (@D25).
    O3  Applications, Runtime and actors
        app({ id, machines }) lists every machine (@D13), optionally with a per-machine wiring
        default: machines: { editor: { machine: EditorMachine, context: { canEdit: SessionRef } } }
        (@D14). The graph is closed and compiled inertly; nothing runs at construction.

        runtimeSetup({ app, services, persistence? }).construct() is synchronous and inert;
        services is an Effect Layer (@D15). runtime.ready() is the only readiness Effect: the first
        call starts one shared bootstrap (validate and prepare persisted data, build the Layer,
        install store and actors providers first, establish silent context baselines, activate,
        then expose handles), later calls join its cached result. Disposal cancels bootstrap and
        closes admission. runtime.runPromise runs Effects with the installed services;
        runPromiseExit is deleted (@D26).

        Actors (@D12):

        - **actorRef(machine, id, { persist?, retain?, context? })**: names a shared actor and 
        declares its wiring once
        - **runtime.ensureActor(ref, { input })**: finds the named actor or creates it; the first 
        accepted input wins
        - **runtime.createActor(machine, { input })**: creates an anonymous local actor, wired by 
        the app default
        - **runtime.disposeActor(actor)**: in-flight commits settle, then the actor is gone
        - **handle ref, send, getSnapshot, snapshots**: the actor's address, commands and reads

        Lifecycle is active, disposing or disposed (@D16). Shared actors live for the Runtime, or
        for retain after their last use, or until disposeActor. send is synchronous admission into
        a bounded mailbox; overflow rejects with AdmissionOverloaded and changes nothing.

        Admission keeps the archived validation: exact app, machine and ref provenance, input,
        complete wiring, compatible providers, cycles and safe-integer headroom are checked before
        any registration or work, and a failure before visibility rolls back in reverse order.

        Actor-to-actor messaging (@D27): an action send(ref, E.X.from(...)) delivers a public event
        to a shared actor as a later FIFO turn of the target, never inside the sender's turn. It is
        a graph edge. A send to a ref with no actor drops the event and reports SendTargetAbsent.
    O4  Context propagates causally complete truth
        Each context slot selects synchronously from one provider snapshot. Reads form an acyclic
        upward graph; a cycle rejects before any actor is admitted. A provider change wakes each
        dependent consumer at most once per settled wave with the latest complete context, never a
        mixed new and old cut from one cause; an equal settlement clears causal debt without an
        event. A blocked context wakeup keeps its FIFO position. A consumer selector defect leaves
        the provider and siblings committed, keeps the consumer's last valid context, publishes one
        issue-only snapshot and retries only on a newer provider revision (@D28).
    O5  Operations: resources, transactions and streams
        resource({ id, key?, lookup, staleTime, gcTime, persist? }), transaction({ id, key?,
        commit, concurrency, persist? }) and stream({ id, key?, subscribe, persist? }) are inert
        descriptors whose adapters receive (params, { signal }) and, for commits, { attempt }
        (@D33). staleTime and gcTime are required Duration.Input values; concurrency is required
        (reject, allow, serialize, cancel) (@D34). A stream adapter returns an Effect Stream (@D35).

        Keys (@D30): the key projector returns a named record, canonicalised with the archived byte
        grammar and bounds (16 levels, 256 nodes, 8,192 UTF-8 bytes); undefined properties are
        absent; an omitted projector is the empty record. invalidate and clear take a family and a
        partial key record and match every entry containing it; tags are deleted.

        Machine use is through static declarations with computed parameters:
        O.x.subscribe(params, { outcomes, placeholder?, when? }) in activities;
        O.x.lookup / refetch / commit / invalidate / clear / setData / cancel in actions. One
        outcomes container serves every family: success, failure (an exhaustive tag-to-event record
        for tagged errors), defect, interrupt and unknown for finite work; value, complete, failure,
        defect, interrupt for continuing work. Each member is optional and maps with a bare event or
        E.X.from(value) (@D31, @D32).

        Commits own their consequences (@D36): commit(params, { optimistic?, writes?, outcomes })
        where writes (setData, invalidate, clear) apply when the commit settles whatever state the
        actor is in, and optimistic writes apply when the commit starts, are seen by every reader of
        that entry, revert on failure or defect, and stay pending on unknown. unknown fires for a
        commit that may have reached the server. attempt.id is minted per attempt (random in
        production, seeded in Stories) and reused on reconciliation.

        Kept from the archived Plans: one canonical store per Runtime; generation fencing of late
        results; pinned parameters and the oldest live binding for automatic refetch; finite work
        only from accepted actions; offline never gates explicit work; invalidate and clear as one
        validated atomic batch of at most 256 identities; the four concurrency policies with
        per-occurrence fencing; honest remote uncertainty (an invoked adapter counts as possibly
        dispatched, cancellation after invocation is unknown, no automatic retry); and stream
        sessions owned per actor with a latest-value projection and no replay.
    O6  Entity domains (tier 1)
        flow/entity-domain.md (final) is normative for this outcome, sections 1 to 9, including its
        recorded-position grammar, the repair rules of section 5 and the checks of section 9.
        flow/entities.md holds its goals and correctness properties C1 to C8;
        flow/entity-domain-examples.md holds seven worked applications. In summary: a
        domain(id, entries) gives plain operations their shared-data meaning (places, conditions,
        orders, pages, predictions, server effects, stream mappings); one record store keeps every
        copy coherent; repair is a join of record deltas and active answers with one-hop observed
        deltas, confirming reads, per-record queues and honest uncertain writes; list membership is
        never predicted (tier 2 is a sync engine, flow/sync-engine-adapter.md, not built).

        On an operation registered in a domain, call-site optimistic and setData are type errors and
        writes may contain only invalidate (@D37). Domain reads are activities like any resource.
    O7  Views and React
        The snapshot is plain frozen data: state, memory, context, issues, lifecycle and activities.
        It has no public revision and no timers (@D38). Every other read is a function applied to a
        snapshot: S.X.is, S.X.child, check(s, event), descriptor.get(s, keyInput) (passive peek of
        a cache entry), and Note.get(s, key, shape) for records.

        Activity lanes (@D39): s.activities.<name> is the lane of the actor's own subscription, a
        _tag union matched with Match.valueTags, always carrying data (undefined when absent) and
        pending (true while an optimistic or predicted write on that entry is unsettled), plus stale
        for domain reads. placeholder is a function ({ previous, input }) => data | undefined.
        Transactions are not read by views; their outcomes become events.

        flow-state/react: FlowProvider({ runtime }), useActorByRef(ref, { input? }) (with input it
        ensures, without it looks up; accepts null), useActor(machine, { input }) (a local actor per
        component, disposed after a short grace period so Strict Mode reattaches), and
        useView(actor, select) as the only read hook, comparing with Equal.equals (@D40). Attaching
        happens in an effect, never in render. Handles, send and event constructors are
        referentially stable. All actors of a Runtime publish into one versioned store, so several
        useView calls in one render see one version. Selector exceptions are memoised per cut.
        useShallow, bound can, O readers and view-model props are deleted. SSR hydration is out of
        scope for version 1; a per-request Runtime with in-memory storage supports server rendering.
    O8  Persistence
        runtimeSetup({ persistence: { scope, version } }) with an Effect KeyValueStore in services
        (@D41). actorRef persist and resource persist select what is stored; transactions and
        streams follow their actor; memory is encoded with the definition's Schemas; entity records
        persist confirmed data only. A second tab on the same scope runs without persistence and
        reports a diagnostic. A different user is a new Runtime.

        Kept from the archived Plan: restore validates and prepares detached data before services;
        restore never replays input, initial, events or finite work; capture observes one
        consistent actor and store cut with a closed durable context graph
        (NonDurableContextProvider is terminal, ConcurrentCapture retryable); writes per scope are
        ordered and a failed write keeps the last good record; pending remote commits restore as
        unknown.
    O9  Stories, fixtures and models (flow-state/testing)
        story.app(setup, { id, fixtures }) targets refs; story.machine(machine, { id, input,
        context?, fixtures }) is the focused kind for a local actor (@D42). Commands: send, process,
        advance, advanceTo, advanceToNextTimer, checkpoint, run; setContext for focused Stories.
        Fixtures are Effect Layers that override service methods. Stories run on the production
        Runtime with the TestClock, seeded ids and a seeded Random; process() is the one explicit
        drain. Checkpoints are atomic cuts carrying snapshots, entity repair evidence and
        diagnostics; reads take the checkpoint (descriptor.get, Domain.entry.get, Note.get,
        Note.queue). CheckpointProvider renders components at a checkpoint. flow.config.ts
        (defineConfig({ apps: [{ app, stories }] })) discovers Stories (@D43).

        model(baseStory, { stateKey }) traverses pure transitions with getShortestPaths and
        getSimplePaths ({ events, maxDepth = 20, limit = 100 }), returning { paths, truncated,
        explored } where explored counts distinct state keys; each path's story replays live.
        propertyTest(domains, { fixture, inputs, seed, runs, steps }) is the entity property test.
    O10  Diagnostics
        One FlowError (@D10) carries a closed code, canonical diagnostics, an optional cause and,
        for Story failures, Story evidence. Diagnostic keeps the archived schema: a real Error and
        Schema.TaggedError with classification Failure, Defect or Interruption, code, path, details
        of scalars, summary and help, rendered safely. The usage vocabulary is regenerated from this
        Plan's surface (adding, among others, SendTargetAbsent, HiddenOrder, HiddenFilter,
        UndeclaredEffect, AdmissionOverloaded; removing codes of deleted surfaces), and every code
        has actionable remediation.
    O11  Inspection, traces and the CLI
        flow-state/inspect exports inspect(app) (the internal representation), render(model,
        "text" | "json" | "mermaid"), attachInspector(runtime, sink) (the supported production
        observer) and trace (import, export) (@D11). The representation contains every structural
        fact without running a callback: states, targets, guards and their possible deny codes,
        operations, outcome edges, activities, schedules, context reads, actor sends, persistence
        opt-ins and the recorded entity domains.

        Trace artifacts use the shared bounded structural codec, carry ordered evidence with
        truncation markers and the entity events of entity-domain.md section 7.4, and redact by
        Schema: a field annotated sensitive is a digest everywhere (@D48). Saved behaviour
        artifacts, share artifacts with path redaction, compression and the long inspect
        restoration list are deleted.

        The CLI binary flow has these leaves (@D11): story list | describe | run, trace summarize |
        diff, graph, diff (two revisions in memory), check, explain. explain covers machines
        (candidate transitions and deny codes, statically or on a checkpoint) and domains
        (entity-domain.md section 7). flow check reports construction errors, id collisions, context
        cycles, persisted consumers of non-persisted providers, the entity rules of entity-domain.md
        section 9 (including the mandatory recorded-position check) as errors, and stuck states,
        unhandled public events, unreachable states and send-then-checkpoint without process() as
        warnings. The CLI keeps the archived host rules: closed grammar, bounded input, atomic
        artifact publication, one result deciding output and exit status.
    O12  Package routes
        Four routes, ESM only:

        - **flow-state**: definition, machine, app, actorRef, runtimeSetup, resource, transaction, 
        stream, deny, check, send, FlowError, entity, domain, read, write, listen, eq, oneOf, 
        contains, between, overlaps, and, serverMatches, principal, asc, desc; types Definition, 
        Machine, App, ActorRef, Actor, Snapshot, Runtime, Diagnostic
        - **flow-state/react**: FlowProvider, useActorByRef, useActor, useView
        - **flow-state/testing**: story, model, defineConfig, CheckpointProvider, propertyTest
        - **flow-state/inspect**: inspect, render, attachInspector, trace

        Everything else is a field inside one of these calls or an Effect primitive (Schema, Layer,
        Schedule, Stream, Match, Duration, KeyValueStore). No deleted name survives as an alias,
        overload or adapter.
    O13  Code disposition
        packages/flow-state-rewrite implements the archived surface (Result returns, "bare" events,
        redirect, reenter, timers, onMemory, contextBindings, Implementation, module) and builds no
        store, operation kernel, persistence, React, Stories, inspection or CLI. Its 795 tests pass.
        It is rebuilt in place on this Plan's surface, layer by layer (@D49):

        - **package shell: routes, build and packed-consumer scripts, tsconfig, lint setup**: keep
        - **operation/key.ts canonicalisation**: port: switch to record keys and partial matching; 
        keep its byte vectors
        - **internal authored-name validation**: port with its vectors
        - **diagnostic schema**: port; regenerate the code vocabulary
        - **runtime-next structural copy, context lineage and waves, evidence journal**: port the 
        algorithms and their behavioural tests into the new runtime
        - **definition, machine, app, implementation, runtime/ (the wired runtime)**: rewrite; 
        delete after replacement
        - **runtime-next/ (unwired)**: delete after its ports land
        - **tests of deleted surfaces**: delete with their modules

        A port keeps the algorithm and its test vectors and changes the surface; no module keeps a
        compatibility shim. Each stage of @O14 leaves the package compiling with its routes
        exporting only finished names.
    O14  Build stages
        Each stage ends at a gate; later stages may start once their prerequisites' gates pass.

        - **S1 Type spike**. builds: the agreed authoring surface without a runtime: definition, 
        internalEvents, .from, outcomes tables, wiring defaults, s.activities, target "self", 
        send(ref), check, schedules; needs: none; gate: @V1
        - **S2 Foundation**. builds: FlowError and diagnostics, names, record keys, structural 
        codec, definition and machine compile, the internal representation and render; needs: S1; 
        gate: @V2
        - **S3 Runtime**. builds: runtimeSetup with Layer services, readiness, refs, ensure, 
        create, dispose, retain, mailbox and macrosteps, schedules, activities, context waves, 
        onContext, actor send, one versioned store, evidence journal; needs: S2; gate: @V3
        - **S4 Operations**. builds: resource store (keys, generations, freshness, gc, lanes, 
        placeholder, invalidate, clear), transactions (concurrency, attempts, writes, optimistic, 
        unknown), streams; needs: S3; gate: @V4
        - **S5 Entity domains**. builds: recording and types (from the draft 8 spike), record 
        store, join, frontiers, consolidation, confirmation, queues, uncertain writes, tombstones, 
        paging; the runtime model ported as the property suite's oracle; needs: S4; gate: @V5
        - **S6 Persistence**. builds: KeyValueStore provider, capture, restore, ordered writes, 
        entity confirmed data; needs: S4; gate: @V6
        - **S7 Testing**. builds: story.app and story.machine, fixtures, process and time, 
        checkpoints and evidence, models, propertyTest, CheckpointProvider, flow.config.ts; needs: 
        S3; entity reads after S5; gate: @V7
        - **S8 React**. builds: FlowProvider, useActorByRef, useActor, useView; needs: S3; gate: @V8
        - **S9 Inspection and CLI**. builds: attachInspector, trace codec and artifacts, the CLI 
        leaves, flow check rules, explain; needs: S3; entity parts after S5; gate: @V9
        - **S10 Proving apps and cutover**. builds: the Dispatch Desk reference and the seven 
        entity examples as runnable apps, a rerun of the agent experiment against the real package, 
        promotion over packages/flow-state, absence of deleted names; needs: all; gate: @V10

        Critical path: S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, then S10. S6, S7, S8 and S9 run in parallel once S3 or S4
        is in place. Workflow Tasks for these stages are created after this Plan is approved.
    O15  What each archived Plan contributes
        - **Statecharts**. kept: identity rules, macrostep order, silent no-ops, pre-commit defect 
        handling, continuing identity, deterministic time; changed: Result returns to throws (@D8), 
        events and memory to Schema (@D44, @D45), flat paths (@D20), nearest handler with 
        fallthrough (@D18), check (@D22), schedules (@D23); deleted: redirect, reenter, timers, 
        onMemory, bound can, the microstep limit, "bare" events
        - **ApplicationsAndActors**. kept: inert closed graph, shared readiness and bootstrap 
        order, admission validation and rollback, causal context, FIFO mailbox, atomic cuts, 
        capacity and headroom; changed: wiring on refs and app defaults (@D14), 
        ensure/create/dispose (@D12), Layer services (@D15), selector-defect policy (@D28); 
        deleted: module, leases, getActor, suspension and prepared states (@D16), public revisions, 
        Implementation, FlowDisposeError
        - **Resources**. kept: canonical key bytes and bounds, one store per Runtime, generations 
        and fencing, passive reads, pinned parameters, offline rule, atomic bounded invalidation; 
        changed: record keys and partial matching (@D30), lanes (@D39), required freshness (@D34), 
        outcomes container (@D31), shared optimistic writes (@D36); deleted: tuple keys, tags, 
        key/getData/getState/cancel readers, the Missing state, actor-local previews
        - **Transactions**. kept: four concurrency policies, per-occurrence fencing, ordinals, 
        honest remote uncertainty, invocation boundary, no automatic retry; changed: required 
        concurrency (@D34), attempt.id (@D33), writes and optimistic (@D36), unknown outcome 
        (@D31), entity record queues (@D37); deleted: transaction readers, the "no completion 
        invalidate" rule, actor-local preview layers
        - **Streams**. kept: per-actor sessions, latest projection, no replay, fencing, persistence 
        without running work; changed: Stream-returning adapters (@D35), outcomes container, 
        activity lanes, persistence follows the actor; deleted: stream readers
        - **ReactAndHosts**. kept: one provider over an existing Runtime, per-request Runtimes, the 
        Effect bridge rule, tear-free selection, memoised selector exceptions; changed: hooks per 
        @D12 and @D40, attachment in effects with a grace period; deleted: render-time preparation, 
        useShallow, bound can, O readers, runPromiseExit, SSR hydration
        - **Persistence**. kept: restore order without replay, consistent capture, durable context 
        closure, ordered last-good writes, uncertain restore; changed: KeyValueStore with scope and 
        version (@D41), entity confirmed data; deleted: persistence(), webStorage, 
        indexedDbStorage, codec, filter, Persistence types, FlowPersistenceError
        - **StoriesAndModels**. kept: production execution, process(), TestClock, seeded ids, 
        atomic checkpoints, models and their bounds; changed: refs as targets, Layer fixtures 
        (@D42), flow.config.ts (@D43), entity evidence and reads, propertyTest; deleted: 
        story.actor, title, description, maxTurns, fixture(), the behavior gateway, 
        FlowStoryExecutionError
        - **DiagnosticsContract**. kept: the Diagnostic schema, classification, safe rendering, 
        remediation per code; changed: one FlowError (@D10), a regenerated code vocabulary; 
        deleted: four error classes and codes of deleted surfaces
        - **InspectionAndArtifacts**. kept: shared bounded codec, ordered evidence with truncation, 
        trace artifacts, defensive bytes; changed: four exports (@D11), entity events, Schema 
        redaction (@D48); deleted: saved behaviour artifacts, share artifacts, compression, the 
        25-name restoration list, trace proof
        - **CommandLine**. kept: closed grammar, bounded input, atomic publication, one result to 
        exit status, installed-binary parity; changed: the leaves of @O11, flow.config.ts 
        selection; deleted: behavior build/render/diff/check, --gateway, trace proof
        - **PackageContract**. kept: four routes, ESM, absence proofs for deleted names; changed: 
        route contents of @O12; deleted: the temporary restoration lists and runtime shell
        - **ProjectDelivery and SurfaceSimplification**. kept: the staged order idea; 
        SurfaceSimplification's settled decisions where not superseded; changed: stages of @O14; 
        superseded decisions named in each decision above; deleted: the approval ceremony and the 
        open rounds, now closed here
decisions
    D1  Structure is data; callbacks only compute values
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D2 and D7. Targets, operations, outcome events, write
        targets and activity identity are static declarations; callbacks compute payloads, memory
        patches, parameters, guard results, selections and write data. Strict, with no escape.
    D2  The machine file is the spec; one representation, renderers on demand
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D3 and D6. No generated spec file is stored.
    D3  One canonical form per concept; correctness first
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D1. Correct on first attempt outranks reviewability,
        which outranks brevity.
    D4  Simplify, do not redesign; every name earns its place
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D10 and minimal-library. A name exists only when an author
        writes it or a tool calls it and nothing else covers it.
    D5  Agents are the primary authors
        Likely mistakes are type errors, flow check errors or diagnostics; when they cannot be,
        they fail in the safe direction (entities.md G7).
    D6  Effect is used where it owns the concept; 4.0.5 is the authority
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D44 to D48: Schema field records, Layer services, Duration
        inputs, Schedule, Stream, Match, KeyValueStore.
    D7  Binding runtime guarantees stay
        Ordered turns, atomic publication, fencing, no replay on restore and honest remote
        uncertainty bind every implementation (SurfaceSimplification C1).
    D8  Authoring returns values and throws FlowError
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D8. Replaces the archived Result returns of Statecharts O1
        and O2.
    D9  Authored identity rules stay
        Kept from Statecharts O1 and ApplicationsAndActors O1: byte limits, rejected code points,
        exact spelling, length-prefixed composite identity, the actor ref wire form.
    D10  One FlowError
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D14. Replaces FlowUsageError, FlowPersistenceError,
        FlowDisposeError and FlowStoryExecutionError.
    D11  Inspect route, CLI leaves and flow check
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D38 to D42, with trace proof deleted (minimal-library
        decision 11) and explain extended to domains (entity-domain.md section 7).
    D12  Actors: shared by ref, local by component; ensure, create, dispose
        Agreed in minimal-library decision 1. Replaces leases, getActor, story.actor and call-site
        contextBindings of ApplicationsAndActors O4 and ReactAndHosts O2.
    D13  module is removed; the app lists machines
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D13.
    D14  Wiring is declared once: on the ref, or as an app default per machine
        Agreed in minimal-library decision 2. Refines SurfaceSimplification D11, which still made
        local actors pass bindings.
    D15  Services are Effect Layers
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D47. Implementation, ImplementationError and the
        succeed/effect/merge values are deleted.
    D16  Lifecycle is active, disposing, disposed; suspension is deleted
        Decided in this Plan. The archived suspended state (ApplicationsAndActors O5) existed for
        React cleanup; decision 1 replaced that with disposal after a grace period, and nothing
        else needs suspension. The prepared state was for render-time preparation, which decision 1
        also removed. Bootstrap phases stay private.
    D17  target "self" means no state change
        Agreed in minimal-library decision 7; the only spelling for staying.
    D18  The nearest handler wins, and guards fall through
        Agreed in minimal-library decisions 7 and 8a. Replaces the archived rejection of the same
        event on an ancestor and a descendant (Statecharts O3). flow graph shows overrides and
        fallthrough.
    D19  Public events and internalEvents
        Agreed in minimal-library decision 4. Sending, decoding or checking an internal event from
        outside is rejected; Stories reach them only through their real sources.
    D20  State paths flatten; tokens expose is and child and narrow types
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D12 and D50, extended by minimal-library 8a.
    D21  Guards return true or deny(code, context?)
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D28.
    D22  check replaces can
        Agreed in minimal-library decision 8. Replaces root and bound can and can(..., { explain }).
    D23  Schedules replace timers; restartOn restarts one schedule
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D53 with restartOn from minimal-library decision 7.
        redirect and reenter are deleted (minimal-library decision 7).
    D24  Hierarchy is acyclic upward reads plus nested states
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D4. No child actors, parallel regions or history states in
        version 1.
    D25  Reactions and producers build payloads with .from
        Agreed in minimal-library decision 5 for outcomes, stream values, onContext and schedules.
        Replaces SurfaceSimplification D23's constructor call with (current, previous).
    D26  runPromiseExit is deleted
        Agreed in minimal-library (deleted or absorbed): runPromise(Effect.exit(...)).
    D27  Actors can send public events to shared actors
        Adopted in this Plan from minimal-library decision 9: asynchronous FIFO delivery, shared
        actors only, public events only, a visible graph edge, no reads.
    D28  A consumer selector defect isolates to that consumer
        Decided in this Plan, closing ApplicationsAndActors Q1 with its candidate behaviour.
    D29  Memory holds keys and drafts, never copies of cache data
        From minimal-library; enforced by a flow check lint for memory written only from a value
        outcome.
    D30  Keys are named records with partial-record invalidation
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D25 to D27. Replaces the tuple keys and tags of Resources
        O1 and O4; the canonical byte grammar and bounds stay.
    D31  One outcomes container; failures map by tag
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D30 and D58, with unknown added (minimal-library decision
        6).
    D32  Outcome members are optional
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D20.
    D33  attempt.id is minted by Flow
        Agreed in minimal-library decision 6. Reverses Transactions O1's "no public identity".
    D34  Concurrency, staleTime and gcTime are required; time inputs are Duration.Input
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D31, D32 and D35.
    D35  Stream adapters return a Stream
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D33.
    D36  Commits own their consequences: writes and optimistic
        Agreed in minimal-library decision 6. Reverses Transactions O1's "no completion-side
        invalidates or clears" and Transactions D2's actor-local previews.
    D37  Entity domains own shared-data policy
        Adopted from entity-domain.md (final), which passed its type spike, agent experiment and
        runtime-model gates. On domain operations, its predictions replace call-site optimistic and
        setData.
    D38  Snapshots keep lifecycle; revisions and timers move to inspection
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D22; timers removed by minimal-library decision 8.
    D39  Activity lanes replace operation readers
        Agreed in minimal-library decisions 8 and 8a, with SurfaceSimplification D57 and D61.
        Replaces key, getData, getState, cancel on readers, the Missing tag and transaction readers
        of Resources, Transactions and Streams O1.
    D40  One read hook, compared with Equal.equals
        Agreed in minimal-library decisions 3, 8 and 8a. Replaces useShallow (deleted by
        SurfaceSimplification D15) and the Object.is laws of ReactAndHosts O3.
    D41  Persistence uses KeyValueStore with scope and version
        Adopted in this Plan from minimal-library decision 10. Replaces SurfaceSimplification D21's
        storage and codec object and the archived webStorage, indexedDbStorage, codec, filter and
        Persistence types.
    D42  Stories target refs; fixtures are Layers
        Adopted in this Plan from minimal-library decision 11. Deletes story.actor, Story title,
        description and maxTurns, and fixture({ implementation, seeds }).
    D43  flow.config.ts discovers Apps and Stories
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D37. Replaces the behavior gateway.
    D44  Event payloads are Schema field records
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D44 and D56. Replaces "bare" and callable event
        declarations.
    D45  Input and memory are Schema field records
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D45.
    D46  Memory requires an initial function
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D59.
    D47  Definitions derive their public Schemas
        Kept from SurfaceSimplification D55.
    D48  Redaction is a Schema annotation
        Decided in this Plan. A field annotated sensitive is a digest in every trace, artifact and
        checkpoint. Replaces the share artifact kind and its path-based redaction
        (InspectionAndArtifacts O5), which was a second mechanism for the same need.
    D49  Rebuild the rewrite package in place; port algorithms, not surfaces
        Decided in this Plan. The package shell and four algorithms carry over with their test
        vectors; every surface is rewritten. Two parallel runtimes and the superseded surface go.
    D50  Version 1 non-goals
        SSR hydration, lazy-loaded features, multi-tab shared persistence, parallel regions,
        machine-spawned child actors, history states, Suspense and error-boundary integration,
        and every tier-2 feature listed in entity-domain.md section 1.2.
constraints
    C1  Archived Plans are provenance only
        Nothing under workflow/plans/archive or workflow/tasks/archive establishes a requirement.
        Where this Plan is silent, an archived rule is not implied; ask and record it here.
    C2  packages/flow-state stays frozen
        It is read for nothing and changed by nothing until S10 promotes the rewrite over it.
    C3  Toolchain
        Use the pinned nub toolchain, Effect 4.0.5 and TypeScript 7; no unpinned dependencies; no
        erased public type information to satisfy a proof.
    C4  Code composition and style
        The code-composition, typescript-style-guide, code-patterns and testing-policy skills
        apply; tests observe behaviour through public boundaries.
verification
    V1  Type spike of the authoring surface
        Establish the type side of @O1, @O2, @O5 and @O7 by compiling the Dispatch Desk editor of
        minimal-library and the examples of @O3 to @O7 without annotations, explicit generics or
        assertions, with negative fixtures for each likely mistake. Record compile time. Planned.
    V2  Foundation
        Establish @O1, @O10 and the structure of @O11 with construction tests, ported name and key
        byte vectors, and an internal-representation golden test proving every target, operation,
        outcome edge, context read and actor send is present without running a callback. Planned.
    V3  Runtime
        Establish @O2 to @O4 with production tests of macrostep order, nearest-handler fallthrough,
        target "self", deny and check agreement, schedule ordering and restartOn, activity identity,
        causal context waves (including the diamond and the selector defect), actor send delivery,
        admission rollback, disposal waiting for commits, and one versioned store cut. Planned.
    V4  Operations
        Establish @O5 with tests of key canonicalisation and partial invalidation, fencing,
        freshness and collection, the four concurrency policies, optimistic writes and their
        revert, writes after settlement in any state, unknown and attempt reuse, and stream
        sessions. Planned.
    V5  Entity domains
        Establish @O6 with the type set of entity-domain.md section 15.1 against the real package,
        golden flow explain output, and the property suite with the ported runtime model as its
        oracle, including its eight caught mutations. Planned.
    V6  Persistence
        Establish @O8 with restore-without-replay, consistent capture, durable context closure,
        last-good writes and the second-tab rule. Planned.
    V7  Testing
        Establish @O9 with Story determinism (identical traces from identical runs), checkpoint
        atomicity and reads, model path bounds and live parity, and CheckpointProvider. Planned.
    V8  React
        Establish @O7 with Strict Mode reattachment, grace-period disposal, stable handles,
        one-version reads across several useView calls, and selector exception memoisation.
        Planned.
    V9  Inspection and CLI
        Establish @O11 with trace round trips and bounds, sensitive-field digests, every CLI leaf's
        output and exit status, and each flow check rule firing on a fixture. Planned.
    V10  Proving apps and cutover
        Establish @O12 to @O14 with the Dispatch Desk and the seven entity examples running as
        applications with Stories, an agent experiment rerun against the real package, packed
        consumers of all four routes, and absence of every deleted name in exports and
        declarations. Planned.
questions
    Q1  Should local actors survive React Activity hiding?
        Activity runs effect cleanups when hidden, so a local actor hidden longer than its grace
        period is disposed. Recommended for version 1: accept it, and add retain to useActor only
        when a real screen needs it.
    Q2  What does invariant-driven development mean here?
        Paused by the user (SurfaceSimplification Q30). Invariants stay a separate function.
    Q3  Entity runtime measurements
        The Runtime-wide repair bound (default 6), audit mode's cost and the property test's budget
        are guesses to measure in S5 (entity-domain.md section 13.2).
